{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "7c8587ac-63e6-8eec-b9af-ac089782612d",
  "created_at": "2026-01-10T10:32:31-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "George Thurston",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:27:55-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works storm line, this is Denise. What's going on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:27:59-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning. My name is George Thurston. I know City Hall is closed today, it is Saturday, so I call this storm line. I hope this is the right number."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:28:10-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You got the right place. We're staffed through the weekend because of the storm. What's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:28:17-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Six ninety-four Thames Street. In the Fifth Ward, down past the Wellington Avenue side. I live there with my fathers."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:28:25-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Six nine four Thames. Okay. Tell me what you're seeing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:28:29-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The storm that came Friday, it finished this morning. Now the whole yard is soaked. The side lot too. And the water, it stands against the foundation of the house. It does not go away. It just sits."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:28:43-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Is any of it getting inside? Basement, anything?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:28:47-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No. No, the house is dry. The basement is dry. I went down this morning and checked. Nothing came in. I want to be clear. This is the yard and the foundation. Not inside."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:29:00-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good, that's good to hear. So it's pooling outside and not draining."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:29:05-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. And I know why. The grate on the corner. The storm drain. It is half full of sand and trash. Cups, bags, sand from the road. Half full. So the water has nowhere to go, it comes back to our yard."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:29:20-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Half blocked, the catch basin at the corner."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:29:24-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. And excuse me, but I have to say this. That grate looks like this since the fall. I walk past it every day. Every day. Nobody cleans it. The city drives the sweeper on Thames, okay, but nobody touches the grate. So when the big storm comes, of course this happens. It is not a surprise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:29:45-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:29:47-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I am not angry with you. But it is a small thing to fix, and nobody fixes it, and now my fathers look out the window at a pond."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:29:58-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. So I'm putting this in as a catch basin backup at the corner by six ninety-four Thames, grate partly filled with sand and debris, standing water in the yard against the foundation, no water in the house. That about right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:30:13-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Can you say it again, please? I want to be sure you have it correct."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:30:19-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. Catch basin backup, corner near six ninety-four Thames Street. Grate about half full of sand and trash. Standing water in the yard and side lot, up against the foundation. House and basement dry."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:30:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. That is correct. When will they come?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:30:36-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Crews are going flat out today on the streets that are actually underwater, so realistically yours is Monday. I'm scheduling it for Monday the twelfth."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:30:46-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Monday. The twelfth. [pause] Okay. Monday. But only cleaning the top is not enough. If they take two bags off and leave, the sand is still there. You understand? I want somebody to look inside the drain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:31:00-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll put that in the notes, that you want the basin itself looked at, not just the grate."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:31:07-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. And also, I would like a supervisor to call me back. Not today, I know today is busy. But somebody who decides. Because if nobody looks at it, this will happen again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:31:20-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can request a supervisor callback. What's the best number for you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:31:25-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "My cell. Four oh one, five five five, oh one five one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:31:30-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four oh one, five five five, zero one five one. Under George Thurston, T-H-U-R-S-T-O-N?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:31:36-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, exactly. Can you repeat the number one time? The line, sometimes it is not good."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:31:43-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four oh one, five five five, zero one five one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:31:47-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. Correct. You know, it is funny. I collect old postcards, vintage ones. Last week I found a rare one, Thames Street maybe nineteen-ten, with the people walking. And in the picture you can see the drain on the corner. A hundred years, the same corner. And in the picture it is clean."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:32:06-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, that's a little embarrassing for us."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:32:09-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A little, yes. So please. Monday, the crew. And the supervisor calls me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:32:14-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Monday for the crew, and the callback request goes in with it. Anything changes before then, water gets near a door or anything, call this line back."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:32:24-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thank you, Denise. I will wait for Monday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-10T10:32:28-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Take care, Mr. Thurston. Stay dry."
    }
  ],
